.th UNAME 1 
.sh NAME
uname \- print system information
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd uname
[
.bd \-a
|
.bd \-m
|
.bd \-p
|
.bd \-r
|
.bd \-s
|
.bd \-v
]

.sh DESCRIPTION
.it uname
prints certain system information. With no options, same as 
.bd \-s.
.s3
The options are:
.s3
.lp +6 5
\fa\*-a\fr	print all information.
.s3
.lp +6 5
\fa\*-m\fr	print machine name.
.s3
.lp +6 5
\fa\*-p\fr	print processor type or "unknown".
.s3
.lp +6 5
\fa\*-r\fr	print the kernel release.
.s3
.lp +6 5
\fa\*-s\fr	print the kernel name.
.s3
.lp +6 5
\fa\*-v\fr	print the kernel version.
